      "writtenOn": "2024-04-24T11:15:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was digging a bit into it. For new edits, the `modificationTarget` is-\n1. Defined [here](https://gerrit.googlesource.com/gerrit/+/refs/heads/master/java/com/google/gerrit/server/edit/ModificationIntention.java#68) to be the current patch set.\n2. Validated [here](https://gerrit.googlesource.com/gerrit/+/refs/heads/master/java/com/google/gerrit/server/edit/ChangeEditModifier.java#799) to have the same change ID as the edited change (i.e. it cannot be a base change).\n3. Then, the [2nd parameter here](https://gerrit.googlesource.com/gerrit/+/refs/heads/master/java/com/google/gerrit/server/edit/ChangeEditModifier.java#418) is passed as the base commit.\n\nAs for this specific test - I tend to say it was buggy. There are quite a few bugs in this test file.",
      "parentUuid": "4515c2d5_7bbbafb3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 425,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 425,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "29004f0e1ab7ab2fd0b5199279f20be30a607507",
